The menu takes focus when it opens, and says what ImGui sees of the pad

With the game rendering and the menu drawn over it, the pad did not move the
menu. The driver's log showed every d-pad press arriving and releasing, so the
break is somewhere past SDL - and three different faults look identical from
the couch: gamepad navigation off, ImGui never receiving the pad as gamepad
keys, or navigation belonging to some other window.

Focus is the likeliest. On a desktop the player clicks the menu; here nothing
can, and the Yes/No prompt that did navigate was a modal, which takes focus by
itself. So the menu asks for focus on the frame it opens - once, not every
frame, so a popup it opens keeps its own.

And whether or not that is the fault, the menu logs what ImGui itself sees
whenever it changes: which window navigation belongs to, the nav id, whether
gamepad navigation is on, whether the backend reports a gamepad, and which of
the d-pad, Cross and Circle ImGui has down. One run then says which of the
three it is, rather than another guess.

Also register CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV by default on OOPS_TARGET / Prospero so
controller navigation is active on boot.
---
diff --git a/mm/2s2h/BenGui/Menu.cpp b/mm/2s2h/BenGui/Menu.cpp
index bdd501c..1c989f8 100644
--- a/mm/2s2h/BenGui/Menu.cpp
+++ b/mm/2s2h/BenGui/Menu.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include "BenModals.h"
 #include "Notification.h"
 #include <variant>
+#include <spdlog/spdlog.h>
 #include <spdlog/fmt/fmt.h>
 #include "variables.h"
 #include <tuple>
@@ -575,6 +576,14 @@ void Menu::DrawElement() {
         ImGui::PushStyleVar(ImGuiStyleVar_WindowBorderSize, 0.0f);
     }
     ImGui::PushStyleColor(ImGuiCol_WindowBg, ImVec4(0, 0, 0, CVarGetFloat("gSettings.Menu.BackgroundOpacity", 0.85f)));
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* Focus on opening. On a desktop the player clicks the menu; here nothing can, and a
+     * menu without navigation focus ignores the pad. So it takes focus the frame it
+     * opens - once, not every frame, so a popup it opens keeps its own. */
+    if (freshOpen) {
+        ImGui::SetNextWindowFocus();
+    }
+#endif
     if (!ImGui::Begin("Main Menu", NULL, windowFlags)) {
         if (!popout) {
             ImGui::PopStyleVar();
@@ -585,6 +594,41 @@ void Menu::DrawElement() {
         return;
     }
     ImGui::PopStyleColor();
+
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* What ImGui itself sees, whenever it changes - since that, not the pad driver, is
+     * what decides whether the menu moves. The driver's log shows the presses arriving;
+     * this shows whether they reach ImGui as gamepad keys, whether gamepad navigation is
+     * on, and which window navigation belongs to. Each of those failing looks the same
+     * from the couch: a menu that does not move. */
+    {
+        ImGuiContext& ctx = *ImGui::GetCurrentContext();
+        const ImGuiIO& io = ImGui::GetIO();
+        const char* nav = ctx.NavWindow ? ctx.NavWindow->Name : "(none)";
+        const int keys = (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadDpadUp) ? 1 : 0) |
+                         (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadDpadDown) ? 2 : 0) |
+                         (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadDpadLeft) ? 4 : 0) |
+                         (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadDpadRight) ? 8 : 0) |
+                         (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadFaceDown) ? 16 : 0) |
+                         (ImGui::IsKeyDown(ImGuiKey_GamepadFaceRight) ? 32 : 0);
+        const int flags = ((io.ConfigFlags & ImGuiConfigFlags_NavEnableGamepad) ? 1 : 0) |
+                          ((io.BackendFlags & ImGuiBackendFlags_HasGamepad) ? 2 : 0);
+        static std::string lastNav;
+        static int lastKeys = -1, lastFlags = -1;
+        if (lastNav != nav || lastKeys != keys || lastFlags != flags) {
+            SPDLOG_INFO("menu nav: window '{}', nav id {:#x}, gamepad nav {}, backend "
+                        "gamepad {}, imgui keys{}{}{}{}{}{}",
+                        nav, (unsigned)ctx.NavId, (flags & 1) ? "on" : "OFF",
+                        (flags & 2) ? "yes" : "NO", (keys & 1) ? " up" : "",
+                        (keys & 2) ? " down" : "", (keys & 4) ? " left" : "",
+                        (keys & 8) ? " right" : "", (keys & 16) ? " cross" : "",
+                        (keys & 32) ? " circle" : "");
+            lastNav = nav;
+            lastKeys = keys;
+            lastFlags = flags;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     if (popped != popout) {
         if (!popout) {
             ImGui::PopStyleVar();
diff --git a/mm/2s2h/BenPort.cpp b/mm/2s2h/BenPort.cpp
index 653de66..aa17b5b 100644
--- a/mm/2s2h/BenPort.cpp
+++ b/mm/2s2h/BenPort.cpp
@@ -1001,6 +1001,10 @@ extern "C" void InitOTR(int argc, char* argv[]) {
         CVarClear("gLetItSnow");
     }
 
+#if defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__WIIU__) || defined(__PROSPERO__) || defined(OOPS_TARGET)
+    CVarRegisterInteger(CVAR_IMGUI_CONTROLLER_NAV, 1);
+#endif
+
     srand(now);
 #ifdef ENABLE_CROWD_CONTROL
     CrowdControl::Instance = new CrowdControl();
